<title>CANADA: United Grain details grain, oilseed output.</title>
<headline>United Grain details grain, oilseed output.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>United Grain Growers, Canada's second largest grain handler, on Wednesday detailed its estimates of grain and oilseed output based on a farmer survey by UGG elevator managers June 2-4, 1997.</p>
<p>			     WESTERN CANADA</p>
<p>	   SEEDED AREA ('000 AC) YIELD (BU/AC) OUTPUT ('000 T)</p>
<p>	 StatsCan 96/7 UGG 97/8 SC96/7 UGG98/7 SC 96/7 UGG 98/7</p>
<p>All Wheat 31,085     27,730    35.7   35.4   29,465  26,404</p>
<p>Oats	 4,785	4,384    68.4   66.9    4,111   3,785</p>
<p>Barley    12,400     12,208    60.2   58.3   14,995  14,733</p>
<p>Rye	    427	  404    29.1   28.0	279     264</p>
<p>Flax	 1,490	2,344    23.4   22.5	843   1,327</p>
<p>Canola     8,802     12,400    25.7   23.5     4,991  6,555</p>
<p>Spc crops  3,391	3,753</p>
<p>Fallow    14,860     14,136</p>
<p>Total     77,240     77,361			 54,685 53,067</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras, Winnipeg Reuters bureau 204 947 3548))</p>
